<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">East Pakistan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1955">1955</a>–<a href="/years/1971">1971</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> was the eastern wing of Pakistan from 1955, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-bengal">East Bengal</a> was renamed, until 1971. Though it held most of Pakistan's population, its people resented political and economic domination by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a>. After the 1970 election and the army's crackdown, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangladesh-liberation-war">Bangladesh Liberation War</a> ended with its independence as Bangladesh in December 1971.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-pakistan.jpg" alt="East Pakistan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mhatopzz · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_Pakistan_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The nuclear programme began in 1972 after the loss of <b>East Pakistan</b>, Abdul Qadeer Khan founded the Kahuta Research Laboratories in 1976 to enrich uranium, and India's tests in May 1998 were answered with Pakistan's own, making it the seventh nuclear-armed state.</blockquote><a href="/empire/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Islamic Republic of Pakistan · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The two successor states remember the struggle in their own ways: India celebrates its independence on 15 August and honours Gandhi as the Father of the Nation, while Pakistan celebrates 14 August and honours Jinnah as its founder; <b>East Pakistan</b> broke away in 1971 to become Bangladesh.</blockquote><a href="/movement/indian-independence-movement">Indian independence movement · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>A cyclone and storm surge struck the coast of <b>East Pakistan</b>, killing perhaps 300,000 to 500,000 people.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-12">12 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>East Bengal became part of the Dominion of Pakistan in 1947 and was renamed <b>East Pakistan</b> in 1955.</blockquote><a href="/state/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a></li></ul></section>
